---
// /docs/troubleshooting — common failure modes + fixes, from real gotchas: reload-gated plugin
// changes, the Node >= 24 requirement and the agentry command off the PATH. Gotchas use .note--warn.
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/docs-layout/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  current="troubleshooting"
  title="Troubleshooting"
  description="Common Agentry failure modes and their fixes: plugin changes that didn't take effect, the Node version requirement, and agentry not found."
  eyebrow="Reference · Troubleshooting"
  lede="The handful of things that trip people up first — what you see, why it happens, and the fix. Most are a reload or a version away from working."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 class="prose__h">Plugin changes didn't take effect</h2>
    <p>
      You edited or updated an agent, command or skill, but the change isn't live in the session.
      These changes are <strong>reload-gated</strong>: they only register on a reload/restart.
    </p>
    <div class="note note--warn">
      <span class="note__key">Gotcha</span>
      <span>
        Agent, command and skill changes register only on a session restart. Restart the
        session, then verify the change live.
      </span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="prose__h">Node version errors</h2>
    <p>
      Agentry requires <strong>Node ≥ 24</strong>. The <code>agentry mem</code> store uses
      <code>node:sqlite</code>, which isn't available on older runtimes, so an older Node fails before
      anything useful happens.
    </p>
    <div class="note note--warn">
      <span class="note__key">Gotcha</span>
      <span>
        Check with <code>node --version</code>. If it's below 24, upgrade Node before launching.
      </span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="prose__h">agentry: command not found</h2>
    <p>
      The plugin puts <code>agentry</code> on the Bash tool's PATH while it is enabled, so a terminal
      outside Claude Code may not have it. The slash commands fall back on their own. By hand, run
      the script it wraps, from the installed plugin's folder, with the same arguments:
    </p>
    <pre class="flag"><code><span class="flag__sigil" aria-hidden="true">$ </span>{'node "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/lane.mjs" exec show T-4'}</code></pre>
    <p>
      <code>CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT</code> is that folder inside Claude Code; in another terminal, put its
      path in. <code>board.mjs</code>, <code>lane.mjs</code> and <code>mem.mjs</code> sit side by side
      in <code>scripts/</code>. <code>agentry --version</code> prints the build that is running.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
